    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I'm doing a quick audit on a new fintech app we're building. Can you give me a checklist of the main WCAG 2.1 requirements I should look for regarding color contrast and screen reader compatibility?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For a WCAG 2.1 audit, here's a checklist of key requirements to focus on for color contrast and screen reader compatibility: \n\n- Color Contrast: \n  - Ensure sufficient color contrast for normal text (ratio of 4.5:1 for heavy text and 7:1 for light text) versus background colors.\n  - Background and text colors have a minimum relative luminance difference of 4.5 (l or 3).\n\n- Screen Reader Compatibility: \n  - Accurate and stable navigation and links.\n  - Clear and distinct language for screen reader labels, such as header hierarchy and form controls.\n  - Enable screen reader access to all hierarchical and semantic HTML elements.",
